<Base title="Credits & sources"><div class="page-shell"><PageHeading title="Made by a community." description="Artwork and writing provenance for this website."/><div class="prose"><h2>Game artwork</h2><p>The homepage background plays a silent loop recorded from the game’s live main-menu colony, without menus, with the native status bars retained. Recorded from the public native release 0.11.6.1 on 18 November 2026, with SDL GPU and High resolution artwork verified after a fresh load, the loop uses a one-second dissolve at the join. Its poster is the exact opening frame. Workers and buildings are drawn by the game itself; no separate unit animations are overlaid.</p><p>{gameplayArtworkCredit}</p><p><a href="https://github.com/Globulation2/glob2">Globulation 2 source repository</a> · <a href="https://github.com/Globulation2/glob2/blob/master/COPYING">Project license</a></p><h2>Handbook screenshots and clips</h2><p>The handbook’s screenshots and silent clips identify the public browser game or released native version used for each capture. Detail images crop those captures to make controls easier to read. The underlying game artwork retains the project’s attribution and GPL license; each chapter records its platform and source context where known.</p><h2>Logo, fonts and pictures</h2><p>The website and online app share the <a href="https://github.com/Globulation2/glob2-design-system">Glob2 design system</a>, including its pinned asset provenance and licenses. The wordmark, the glob icon, the colony scene, and the building, flag and resource pictures are the game’s own artwork (<code>data/gfx</code>, <code>data/highres</code>, <code>data/icons</code>), prepared for the web by the game repository’s <a href="https://github.com/Globulation2/glob2/blob/master/services/online/apps/web/art/README.md">web art script</a> and licensed with the game under the GPL 3. Titles use Glob2 Sans, the game’s DejaVu Sans–based font (<a href="/fonts/LICENSE-DejaVu.txt">licence</a>); text uses Nunito (SIL Open Font License, <a href="/fonts/LICENSE-Nunito.txt">licence</a>).</p><h2>Article media viewer</h2><p>The article viewer uses <a href="https://github.com/dimsemenov/PhotoSwipe">PhotoSwipe 5.4.4</a>, by Dmitry Semenov, under the <a href="/licenses/LICENSE-PhotoSwipe.txt">MIT license</a>. The library provides zoom, pan, touch gestures and gallery navigation.</p><h2>Legacy writing</h2><p>Guide and archive pages link to their original sources. Where reuse rights have not been established, this site provides a source link and an independently written summary rather than republishing the article.</p><a href="/archive/">Explore the archive →</a></div></div></Base>
